-- title:
--   Closed subschemes of Pⁿ_A from finitely generated homogeneous ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, $A$ a commutative ring, and $I$ an ideal of the polynomial ring $A[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ in $n+1$ variables. Assume $I$ is homogeneous in the sense that for every $p \in I$ and every degree $d$ the $d$-th homogeneous component of $p$ again lies in $I$, and assume $I$ is finitely generated. Let $\mathcal{I}$ be ideal sheaf data on $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the standard grading of $A[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ by homogeneous submodules, and suppose that for each index $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ the ideal assigned by $\mathcal{I}$ to the affine open $D_+(X_i)$ (affine because $X_i$ is homogeneous of degree one and $1 > 0$) is the ideal generated by the sections obtained, via the canonical map from the degree-zero homogeneous localisation away from $X_i$ to sections over $D_+(X_i)$, from the fractions $F/X_i^{d}$ with $F \in I$ homogeneous of degree $d$, for all $d$ and all such $F$. The conclusion is that the composite of the closed immersion $\mathcal{I}.\mathrm{subschemeι}$ of the associated closed subscheme into $\mathbb{P}^n_A$ followed by the structure morphism $\mathbb{P}^n_A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is locally of finite presentation.
--
--   This records that a closed subscheme of projective space over $A$ cut out chart-by-chart by a finitely generated homogeneous ideal is locally of finite presentation over $A$, the finiteness half of the standard description of such subschemes; the charts are handled through the identification of the degree-zero localisation away from $X_i$ with a polynomial algebra over $A$ on the ratios $X_k/X_i$. It feeds the construction of points of the Hilbert functor, where the subscheme cut out by a homogeneous ideal is exhibited as a flat, locally finitely presented closed subscheme with prescribed kernel ideal.
